  "narrative": "The new evidence separates into two clear outcomes. First, the stringent screen-quality filter (screen_roc_auc >=0.94 and cas9_activity_pct >=70%) confirms the four principal dependency associations: H208 SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency is +0.743 [0.638,0.847], H209 KEAP1-loss weaker dependency is +0.730 [0.633,0.828], H210 TP53-loss weaker dependency is +0.382 [0.249,0.516], and H211 MSI-high stronger dependency is +0.720 [0.564,0.876]. All lower bounds are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, so these context-robust dataset-internal associations are accepted and closed. This QC robustness is scientifically reassuring because screen_quality and Cas9 activity could otherwise confound or dilute observed dependencies, but it does not establish causality or external generalizability.\n\nSecond, PTEN-loss scope remains unresolved. H207, the broad stringent-quality PTEN-loss contrast, is +0.131 [-0.007,0.270] in the claimed direction; the point estimate is below the practical threshold and the interval includes zero, so I reject that specific claim of a robust PTEN association under the stringent broad filter. This does not overturn the previously accepted overall PTEN-loss association or accepted high-IFN/clean-context PTEN associations, but it prevents extending PTEN robustness to that technical filter. H202, the clean low-IFN PTEN-loss direct contrast, is +0.206 [0.119,0.293]. The point estimate exceeds the threshold and the interval excludes zero, but the lower bound is materially below threshold, so I keep it unresolved rather than accepting threshold-scale robustness. It is the most informative current evidence that PTEN-loss may not be confined to high-IFN contexts, but it is not decisive.\n\nThe clean high-IFN TP53-loss contrast H201 is +0.354 [0.144,0.563]. It is clearly directionally supportive and excludes zero, but the lower bound is just below the 0.15 threshold. Given the smaller exposed cell and the need to distinguish attenuation from imprecision, I leave it unresolved/active rather than declaring threshold-decisive context support. H200, the corresponding IFN-gamma interaction for TP53-loss, is not supported (+0.147 opposite direction with interval crossing zero), so there is no evidence from this test for additional high-IFN attenuation beyond the main TP53-loss association. H199 similarly rejects a positive IFN-gamma interaction for KEAP1-loss. These interaction tests are secondary and multiplicity-sensitive; the new results argue against strong IFN-driven modification of KEAP1 or TP53 effects in this dataset.\n\nThe MYC-expression interaction tests are mixed and do not support decisive modifier claims. H184 SMARCA4-loss MYC interaction is negative in the signed direction (-0.098 [-0.247,0.052]) and is rejected. H186 TP53-loss MYC interaction is positive +0.283 [0.089,0.476], but the lower bound is well below threshold and close to zero; I leave it unresolved/deferred rather than accept an interaction claim without validation, especially because the direct TP53 main effect is already well supported across multiple contexts. H212, the clean PTEN-loss high-IFN interaction, is +0.186 [-0.028,0.400]; despite a nominally above-threshold point estimate, the interval includes zero and is imprecise, so I reject this interaction claim.\n\nValidation budget is exhausted, so acceptance cannot be strengthened by new independent replication. I therefore keep direct threshold-limited context results unresolved, reject null or subthreshold direct/interaction results, and accept only the stringent-filter confirmations that are decisively threshold-clear. The registered follow-up proposals are designed to resolve the remaining threshold-limited direct questions by increasing cell sizes in targeted ways: clean TP53-loss with a relaxed elevated-IFN threshold and clean low-IFN TP53-loss, plus a broad low-IFN PTEN-loss test with high screen quality. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal claims or external generalizations.",
  "research_notes": "Updated through iteration 12 appraise. Dataset-internal robust associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency; KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker dependency; MSI-high -> stronger dependency. These main effects remain robust in stringent screen-quality/Cas9 filters (H208-H211 accepted and closed). PTEN loss is modestly accepted overall and accepted in several targeted contexts including high IFN and clean genomic backgrounds, but PTEN scope is unresolved: clean low-IFN PTEN H202 is +0.206 [0.119,0.293], point above threshold but lower bound below threshold; stringent broad PTEN H207 is not supportive (+0.131 [-0.007,0.270]). TP53 high-IFN clean direct H201 is +0.354 [0.144,0.563], unresolved threshold-limited; IFN interaction H200 rejected, arguing against additional high-IFN modification. KEAP1 IFN interaction H199 rejected. MYC interaction H184 rejected, H186 unresolved/deferred due subthreshold lower bound and multiplicity. Clean PTEN high-IFN interaction H212 rejected. Validation budget exhausted. Next plan: use relaxed elevated-IFN and low-IFN clean TP53 direct tests to distinguish imprecision from attenuation, and broad low-IFN high-screen-quality PTEN test to assess PTEN breadth. Do not accept interactions unless decisively threshold-clear. Maintain no causality or generalizability claims."
